{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_45f6186c1729a04a722d29291a00a6a37b21a80b82ea1f4b40ce4e9552b2e878","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_59abafa86d862b17671e0a9e4fe8d6e58f51adc83a5b7016c3617d8a9fadc23c","slc_a1530b69ea7cd700ed8545653f853b117df64ec0690c7cec01dab229c51b49dd"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"The README reports a benchmark comparing OpenDev 0.1.4 startup (4.3 ms), peak memory (9.4 MB), and install size (18 MB) against Codex, Claude Code, and OpenCode on macOS ARM64 using hyperfine and /usr/bin/time.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4a036e3fd12f5f820c20bda1de179af88b26e18466b98ba789a5d1ca8f6622c2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_058c583ebab0c74e19cc2c30b906bdb7e2c190c09c9e0b8dccf2c96a61d72b52","slc_9fb05c90980cdb5022c956e78a9258317912a14dd8bc631e2054d877af948407","slc_fd8f851b723ae90c4debadb91258864408d2f6b5caeb21a61f8e22e6e31e0376"],"source_ids":["src_e62a0f140c195ff18f1a3c740c59bbb3"],"text":"Per-agent sidechain transcripts are stored as append-only JSONL at `~/.opendev/sessions/{session_id}/agents/{agent_id}.jsonl`, with readers that filter malformed lines and orphaned tool calls for resume.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4be6dda976e36c638f39a11f9cbb51907212a6cd5dbe269efe3e4f4de1989042","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2574c5ff1197b1f42fdf29092c795d9fb76c4800198a831a79b788e0f2d6bbb4","slc_a177860ba91764e32f3ddc1b97c10fa7c15343bfbe60a03a4d364d3c95e1522c"],"source_ids":["src_e62a0f140c195ff18f1a3c740c59bbb3"],"text":"A WorktreeManager creates git worktrees per agent (branch `opendev/agent-{short_id}`), detects changes, and removes clean worktrees while preserving dirty ones for review.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_503fccdc1b8c9488d684ace2158f9b123df837d07cd7016bbd32d16ffbc7ad8b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03de7a87651956b90e20890fd93ff41a1ac671a045fac34de7b3cfd3dce717ff","slc_04ee688982409993140b6023f6d5c08a340e61002dca19e7469f141f97a1a4fe","slc_63b8b02fdc9f841281f16392bab7272a0b33d7605ad5adfda4775f5c9b484951","slc_73b4fb7b24098a828769662ac74c77c4977281e6af3185bcfeaf77b4a241ea1d","slc_85c1d8f5ad79ea7415123441768c0e75401eef9e74fa4309bd67b7f7fda343e5"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"The CLI offers an interactive TUI (`opendev`), a Web UI (`opendev run ui`), single-prompt mode (`-p`), session resume (`--continue`), and an interactive `opendev config setup` for provider/model binding.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5311f4defdac0b9aa5585ce7580bda67b36fcaf7da683781a35d43a68074b1a6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3816c67b6c771a6bbe54c8ee484d15f7bc0959b4afb0a9bef2d0b73aab0bb8f4","slc_f98e485598eaf0fbb0728fd4339d047d3f0621321bb9b3893f547cdaea48937c"],"source_ids":["src_e62a0f140c195ff18f1a3c740c59bbb3"],"text":"The design doc specifies a TaskManager in opendev-runtime: a UI-agnostic task lifecycle state machine with idempotent transitions, a notified flag, 5-second eviction grace, and retain-to-block-eviction.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_587ad963f0b29c88ef84f12dcef9d4ea5191f60cd22ff4e50b88e648d835bf9d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_df79ed3f8501b820c9cd8166e14d9c1a4987b07f50f653d00648e005af761b14","slc_e551e3cdf98800828ff5e809e3d8a1fef8f63b4c6ee8beb54512eb80931e891d"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"Five workflow slots are defined: Normal (execution), Thinking (reasoning), Compact (context summarization), Critique (self-critique), and VLM (vision), each bindable to any configured LLM.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5ef3258e920f6d4f26c73241dd365762485d0daf361f457820279bbaa4b492f8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8cfcef0aa6b5561027c7ac3c16527c04662d4e27af0d609fded0b93e02044f40","slc_9af16f8ea22ba5d713c809b32e715e7b0c06d28f80cc0ea869f00da5716acf55","slc_cd67f7c1177d4aefc87ce7e277ec9ad06e8bf067e348a909a46ba9599f768eab"],"source_ids":["src_e62a0f140c195ff18f1a3c740c59bbb3"],"text":"A file-based mailbox system gives each agent an inbox with fd-lock protocol, corruption recovery via rename, a 1000-entry cap, and message types including Text, ShutdownRequest, ShutdownResponse, and Idle.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_69a59e544af4ec3feac0eff2c0f1723abb9883b424d2764fbce30d77686750c1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d8b5ffe54cc86d9281223cccacbaa71380d303f77111a1e2f0a034ee69071d0","slc_f0021ac170972336418975ff3b5e87904728324b3df4aa0618be0d70397cd4fe"],"source_ids":["src_e62a0f140c195ff18f1a3c740c59bbb3"],"text":"A `run_in_background` parameter on `spawn_subagent` returns a task_id immediately, runs the agent in a detached tokio task, and injects results into the parent via a sentinel mechanism when idle.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a37a5639b9500601d35921738382ebbdd7c5d31c459de9de01bc5a720a5aa074","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_df79ed3f8501b820c9cd8166e14d9c1a4987b07f50f653d00648e005af761b14"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"Workflow slots have documented fallback behavior: Thinking and Compact fall back to Normal, Critique falls back to Thinking, and VLM falls back to Normal when the model lacks vision.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a7ea034be18177b69b9c1a56b4d0f55a061c21db4ad2a8403a5d5abee745b940","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8a62a4af0f56274cf1dfb6d58a12c969929dd9bcd39642a88407c271ea73ba3d"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"The agent supports nine LLM providers: OpenAI, Anthropic, Fireworks, Google, Groq, Mistral, DeepInfra, OpenRouter, and Azure OpenAI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b679802c5a694a0347f7891060e029565b37b2bd707da0f957abf9949251ecab","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"opendev-to/opendev@d32c660e4eed snapshot 6c2de2a3889db931","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ad72b3f9644db13de1561ca1084aec15f3366cde3d8727b674c372f7bdfaca2e","slc_d703161ba259f1d23985faeb9fb89bf7a63c80dccee676dfb076e5e238ae265b"],"source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"text":"An agent fleet can launch multiple sub-agents in parallel, each with its own LLM binding, context window, and tool access, aggregating results back into the session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
